      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original with its own preparation disclosed; no current English original read. Four complete khas ma blangs denials retain the attested not our position idiom with four distinct English occurrences; the final positive assertion has only a negative seeing predicate. The prior-position phrase is contextually original position, while contrary opponent glossary variants remain evidence, not a source correction. The common-locus expression is distributed across one thing that is three different things and is omitted; its existing auto-aligned wet and flowing glossary is not used to steal the earlier properties. The singular gcig is represented by an English indefinite article and is omitted without inventing one. Two fluids compounds keep strictly tighter pus/blood members, with English member order reversed. Final karma and causal-control phrase stay flat with his unwrapped, despite positive broader HGM19353 wording. First yang and the active agentives have no separate exponent; the final yi dvags kyi role is preserved verbatim with no silent conversion to kyis. The opening bracketed explanation and supplied particles/participants remain unwrapped. No source or hgm_gloss changes or human certification are implied; skeptical review remains required."
